/polyemesis
# `go build ./scripts/cmd/gotest/` drops its binary in the working directory,
# which is the repository root, and 2.7MB of it very nearly went into a commit
# about not letting things pass unnoticed.
/gotest
/dist/
/data/
node_modules/
ui/dist/
config.yaml

# The built UI is a build artefact, not source. But go:embed requires the
# directory to contain at least one file or `go build ./...` fails in a clean
# checkout -- hence the tracked .gitkeep. The `all:` prefix on the embed
# pattern is what makes go:embed match a dotfile.
internal/web/dist/*
!internal/web/dist/.gitkeep

*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Key material, by NAME rather than by location.
#
# /data/ above already covers the default layout, but it is anchored to the
# repository root and dataDir is configurable. Point it at ./test-data to run a
# second instance and secret.key — the NaCl secretbox key that decrypts every
# stored OAuth token and stream key — lands somewhere nothing ignores.
#
# *.db is already unanchored, so the database is safe wherever it is written.
# The key that decrypts its contents was not. These names are fixed in the
# code: config.SecretPath and internal/tlsx's self-signed set.
secret.key
ca.key
server.key
*.pem
.DS_Store
.playwright-mcp/

# Agent working notes: progress state, session hand-off, scratch analysis.
# Deliberately untracked -- these are notes-to-self about how the work is
# going, not artefacts of the project, and they go stale the moment the work
# they describe lands.
.work/
.docker-gocache/
.docker-gomod/

# Agent scratch. Same reasoning as .work/ above: notes about how the work is
# going, not artefacts of it.
#
# .claude/worktrees holds git worktrees INSIDE the repository, so leaving it
# tracked would commit an entire second checkout into the tree.
.claude/
.superpowers/

# Presentation material: slides for a video or a talk, built from the docs but
# not part of them. Regenerated freely and often half-finished, and a deck is
# not something a reader of this repository needs in order to run polyemesis.
presentation/

# Playwright's own trace/video output from the capture harness. 18 MB of
# .webm per run, regenerated every time, and it lands INSIDE docs/media
# because that is where the harness writes — so it is one `git add -A` away
# from history unless it is named here.
docs/media/.playwright/

# The built site. `/dist/` above is root-anchored and does not cover it, so
# without this line web/dist ships a second copy of every screenshot and the
# 1.4 MB tour video that web/public already holds.
web/dist/

# Internal working documents. They stay on disk and are deliberately not
# tracked, because this repository is public and "not linked from the website"
# is not the same property as "not on the internet".
#
# Directories rather than filenames ON PURPOSE. A public .gitignore is itself
# published, so a list of individual filenames would be an index of exactly the
# material this is meant to withhold -- and every one of them is still reachable
# in this repository's history, which is where that index would point.
docs/internal/
docs/superpowers/
docs/security/
docs/notes/

# docs/evidence/ is NOT here, deliberately. It holds the handful of notes
# that public pages cite as the source for a factual claim -- the competitor
# table's receipts, the Enhanced RTMP findings README depends on. Those have
# to stay readable or the claims lose their evidence, which is worse than
# either publishing or removing them cleanly.
coverage.out
ui/coverage/
web/coverage/
.gitnexus

# Astro build cache and dev log. Regenerated on every build; dev.log in
# particular churns on every run.
web/.astro/
